    <h2>Think about riding on a horse?</h2>
    <p>
        Riding a horse is a timeless experience, where rhythm, connection, and freedom create lasting memories.
    <br />
        This page is about the basics of horseback riding.
    </p>

    <br />

    <h2>🐾 Why Ride Horses?</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>It builds a strong bond between human and animal</li>
        <li>It improves balance, coordination, and confidence</li>
        <li>It’s a peaceful way to connect with nature</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>🧭 Types of Horseback Riding</h2>
    <p>
        There are many styles of riding. Here are a few popular ones:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>English Riding: Used in shows and competitions. Riders sit upright and use a flat saddle.
        <br />
            <img width="15%" src="Pics/EnglishRidingPic.png" />

        </li>
        <li>Western Riding: Common in the U.S., with a larger saddle and more relaxed posture — often seen in cowboy movies!
        <br />
            <img width="15%" src="Pics/WesternRidingPic.png" />
        </li>
        <li>Trail Riding: Riding through nature, forests, or fields. Great for beginners and peaceful adventures.
            <br />
            <img src="Pics/TrailRidingPic.png" />

        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>🧠 What I’ve Learned So Far</h2>
    <p>
        Even though I’m still a beginner, I’ve learned that horses are sensitive and smart. They feel your energy. When you’re calm — they’re calm.
    Riding isn’t just about control — it’s about trust.
    </p>

    <h2>📸 My Dream</h2>
    <p>
        One day, I hope to ride regularly, maybe even own a horse. Until then, I’ll keep learning, dreaming, and sharing my passion here.
    </p>







